<title>UK: NatWest Securities hires three from SBC Warburg.</title>
<headline>NatWest Securities hires three from SBC Warburg.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>NatWest Securities said on Thursday it had hired a team of three specialist equity salesmen from rival investment bank SBC Warburg to cover UK and European equity sales to Scandinavian investors.</p>
<p>The recruitment of Patrick Rarden, Mogens Rye and Peter Kysela move comes after NatWest hired Michael Mortensen from Paine Webber to cover sales of U.S. equities to Scandinavian institutions.</p>
<p>&quot;We are delighted to welcome such a high calibre team of sales professionals,&quot; said NatWest head of UK and European institutional sales Nick Bowers.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom, +44 171 542 5106</p>
